<title>RUSSIA: Russian Rosneft 1996 oil output up to 13.1 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russian Rosneft 1996 oil output up to 13.1 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian state oil holding firm NK Rosneft boosted crude oil output in 1996 to 13.1 million tonnes from 12.8 million in 1995, a company statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>It provided the following preliminary details for the company, which is slowly being privatised:</p>
<p>				1996		 1995</p>
<p>Crude oil output</p>
<p> (million tonnes)	 13.10		12.80</p>
<p>Natural gas output	 5.16		 4.94</p>
<p>(billion cubic</p>
<p>metres)</p>
<p>Refining operations	4.78		 4.88</p>
<p>(million tonnes)</p>
<p>Crude oil exports	  5.75		 4.90</p>
<p>(million tonnes)</p>
<p>New drilling (metres)   472,200		n/a</p>
<p>New pipelines (km)	648		    n/a</p>
<p>New reservoir capacity  47,000		 n/a</p>
<p>(cubic meters)</p>
<p>Note -- Rosneft did not provide breakdowns for refining operations or for subsidaries and units. The joint-stock company is the Russian government's official agent in all oil production-sharing deals. Its leading holdings include the Purneftegaz and Sakhalinmorneftegaz oil production units. Its Krasnodar refinery declared bankruptcy in December 1996.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
